  "decision": "User decision 2026-09-30: default zero-point provider constrained (symmetric get_full(N) mesh, no regularization); at the zone centre only the constrained soft pair is removed; the orbit axis reaches the provider through an optional keyword axis.",
  "scope": "Replace the removal of the whole zone centre in LSWTZeroPointEnergy(method=\"constrained\") by the removal of the orbit-rotation mode only.",
  "principle": "The constrained coordinate is the uniform rotation about the orbit axis, one boson mode at k = 0. Its curvature is the classical one along the orbit (already in E_cl, negative on part of a tilted path), the linear term dropped on the soft path couples only to it, and its zero-point energy belongs to the quantization of phi in Gamma, not to Gamma. The other zone-centre bands are gapped fluctuations and stay. With the rotation angle read by least squares, the removed phase-space pair is span{t, J t}, the boson line u_i = sqrt(S_i)(t_theta,i + i t_phi,i) in the local frame (e_theta, e_phi, s_i); H(k = 0) is restricted to its orthogonal complement by a block unitary diag(Q, conj(Q)), which keeps the paraunitary structure.",
  "changed": {
    "code-space/spintoolkit/methods/state_selection.py": "LSWTZeroPointEnergy.__call__(..., axis=None) with accepts_axis = True; _soft_boson_line, _harmonic_zero_point; select_on_manifold and orbit_energy_landscape pass axis= to providers with accepts_axis (3-argument providers unchanged); without axis the whole zone centre is dropped and describe() records it; the provider description is recorded after the E_qm evaluation",
    "code-space/tests/test_methods/test_state_selection.py": "3 tests: u (not its conjugate) is the D17 null vector of H(0) with the problem rotated off z; projection with the axis and whole-zone-centre removal without it; a 3-argument provider still works",
    "examples/nbcp_effective_potential_check.py": "the prototype passes axis = z to the provider"
  },
  "convention_check": "Y (J_PD) with the whole problem rotated off z: |H(0)(u, conj u)| / |H| = 2.2e-16, and 0.13 for the conjugate line (V: 3.5e-16 and 0.11).",
