  "findings": [
    "The discretization error of the Brillouin-zone sum dominates the mesh dependence; the zone-centre treatment is a smaller correction. Y 1.7 degrees: |shift| N = 6/12/18 = 8.317e-3/8.389e-3/8.395e-3 (zone centre dropped) and 8.369e-3/8.403e-3/8.401e-3 (soft pair projected). Y 5.7 degrees moves by 7e-3 rad between N = 6 and 18 with either treatment, so larger tilts need N >= 12.",
    "Zero tilt against the independent N = 48 scans: amplitude and curvature ratios at N = 6 improve from 1.007 to 1.0000 (J_Gamma) and from 1.018 to 1.011 (Y J_PD); all 16 NBCP verdicts, the 36 criteria verdicts and the 8 benchmark verdicts are unchanged.",
    "Implementation against the independent 72-point prototype (both with the projection): within 2.2e-3 rad in every selected case (largest: Y 5.7 degrees).",
    "Y 16.7 degrees: adiabatic ratio 0.023, below the warning threshold 0.1.",
    "V 0.57 degrees at N = 18: 6 unstable mode pairs on part of the path with either treatment (long-wavelength soft branch where the classical curvature along the orbit is negative); the real part of the frequencies is used and the count is logged. It grows with the mesh density."
  ],
